27. WebFlux Adoption Scenario
Question

When should you NOT use WebFlux?

Answer

When:

Application is mostly CPU bound
Everything is blocking
Low traffic system
Interview One-Liner
WebFlux is not a silver bullet.


28. Throughput Scenario
Question

Throughput requirement is 25k TPS.

Answer

Consider:

WebFlux
Netty
Reactive stack
Interview One-Liner
Reactive architecture targets high throughput use cases.


29. Real-Time Banking Scenario
Question

Transactions must be streamed to fraud detection immediately.

Answer
REST API
    |
Kafka
    |
Reactive Consumer

Interview One-Liner
Reactive streaming is ideal for real-time processing.


30. Most Important Senior-Level Question
Question

If external APIs and database are still blocking, does adopting WebFlux automatically make the application reactive?

Answer
No


WebFlux helps only when the entire call chain is non-blocking.


Ultimate One-Liners
Mono = 0 or 1 item.
Flux = 0 to N items.
WebClient replaces RestTemplate.
Netty is the default reactive server.
Backpressure protects slow consumers.
Blocking code kills WebFlux scalability.
flatMap = parallel processing.
zip = combine async calls.
Reactive works best with R2DBC + WebClient.
WebFlux shines for high-concurrency I/O-bound systems.
